<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="46.2" level="1">Motor Vehicles</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="IV" level="2">Dealers and Driver Training Schools</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="15" level="3">Motor Vehicle Dealers</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="4" level="4">Conduct of Business</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>46.2-1535</section_number>
	<catch_line>Advertisements</catch_line>
	<text>
		Unless the dealer is clearly identified by name, whenever any licensee places an advertisement in any newspaper or publication, the abbreviations "VA DLR," denoting a Virginia licensed dealer, shall appear therein.
	</text>
	<history>1988, c. 865, § 46.1-547.10; 1989, c. 727; 1991, c. 117.</history>
</law>
